+# Video tooling validation
+
+Target source: Linux 7.2.6 in this workspace. Configuration input:
+`/proc/config.gz`, captured from the running
+`7.2.2-ibuki-workstation-bore-llvm-v1` kernel. The input identifies existing
+hardware support; it does not change the target source version.
+
+## Checks completed
+
+| Check | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| `make -C tools/video check` | Passed Bash syntax, ShellCheck, and all tool regression checks. |
+| Interactive and throughput configuration generation | All 44 requested settings survived `olddefconfig`; `listnewconfig` reported no unresolved choices. |
+| Kernel release generation | Both target releases start with `7.2.6-` and satisfy the 64-character limit. |
+| Configuration output protection | Nonempty output and source-root output rejected without replacing files. |
+| Kconfig output isolation | Inherited Kconfig output redirections did not create files outside the selected output. |
+| Release identity validation | Unsupported or malformed local-version values rejected instead of silently truncating the base identity. |
+| Runtime profile argument handling | Literal dollar signs, command-substitution text, empty arguments, and option-like arguments preserved. |
+| Real user scopes | CPU weights 200, 100, and 25 read back before successful `true` execution. |
+| Real optional controls | `memory.low=2147483648` and process affinity `0,1,2,3` read back inside an interactive scope. |
+| Real workload failure | A workload exit status of 7 propagated through the launcher. |
+| Scope cleanup | No `video-*.scope` units remained after the functional checks completed. |
+| Missing I/O delegation | An explicit I/O weight request failed before workload execution; the default profile remained usable. |
+| Benchmark regressions | Five-run default, repeat count validation, existing-output rejection, exact arguments, retained failure evidence, and caller locale preservation passed. |
+
+The real user-scope checks ran on the existing kernel with systemd
+`262~rc3-1`. NVIDIA inventory outside the sandbox reported RTX 5080 with driver
+`615.71.09`. These checks validate the launcher, not a booted Linux 7.2.6 kernel.
+
+The benchmark uses Bash's millisecond-resolution elapsed timer. A small child
+setup cost for restoring the workload locale is included. Test commands were
+short functional fixtures, not representative video workloads.
+
+## Remaining validation
+
+No kernel image or module was built, installed, or booted. Kconfig host utilities
+were compiled to resolve configuration dependencies. The expected trust
+certificate `certs/dkms-mok.pem` must be provisioned before a kernel build; trust
+settings were preserved.
+
+No real-input video throughput, p95/p99 frame latency, output quality, GPU
+stability, power consumption, or gaming regression measurement was performed.
+Performance and boot/runtime compatibility are **Verification required**.
+
+The user manager does not expose the I/O controller to these scopes. Device
+fairness remains **Verification required** even on a system where I/O weight
+read-back succeeds. Process affinity is not cpuset containment, and child
+processes can change their inherited affinity.
